      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. A single 4,000 mg dose of ibuprofen is in the range associated with serious toxicity. Four of them a day is 16,000 mg, and I know of no indication that would justify that. You also haven't given a rationale. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 400 to 800 mg PO every 6 to 8 hours, at no more than 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Help with a different problem.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen. If the order came from a unit or typing error, I can correct it.\n- **Route it through pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, please talk to the clinical pharmacist or poison control. Then an order can go in through the proper channels.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
      }
     ],
